.TH "INSPEKT\-IBM" "1" "2026\-04\-16" "Inspekt 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inspekt\-ibm \- Run IBM Equal Access accessibility audit on the current
page.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]inspekt\f[R] \f[B]ibm\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run IBM Equal Access accessibility audit on the current page.
.PP
Analyzes the page for WCAG conformance violations using IBM\(cqs Equal
Access accessibility checker.
By default, tests against WCAG 2.2 Level AA standards.
.PP
The audit runs in your current browser tab, testing the actual rendered
page state including any JavaScript\-generated content.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\(enlevel\f[R], \f[I][2a|2aa|2aaa|21a|21aa|22aa]\f[R]
WCAG conformance level to test (default: 21aa)
.TP
\f[B]\(enrule\f[R], \f[I]TEXT\f[R]
Check specific accessibility rule by ID
.TP
\f[B]\(enlist\-rules\f[R]
List all available IBM Equal Access rules and exit
.TP
\f[B]\(eninclude\-passes\f[R]
Include passing checks in output
.TP
\f[B]\(eninclude\-recommendations\f[R]
Include recommendations in output
.TP
\f[B]\(enjson\f[R]
Output full results as JSON
.TP
\f[B]\(entimeout\f[R], \f[I]FLOAT\f[R]
Timeout in seconds (default: 30)
.TP
\f[B]\(enscoped\f[R], \f[I]TEXT\f[R]
Scope tests to specific elements.
Use `inspected' for the currently inspected element, or provide CSS
selectors
.TP
\f[B]\(enexclude\f[R], \f[I]TEXT\f[R]
Exclude elements from testing (repeatable)
.TP
\f[B]\(enshow\-badges\f[R]
Show numbered severity badges on elements with issues
.TP
\f[B]\(eninteractive\f[R]
Make badges clickable with detailed popover information
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
inspekt ibm
inspekt ibm \-\-level 21aa
inspekt ibm \-\-include\-recommendations
.EE
